 "text": "Hey, good to have you chat. How are you? Totally normal. The key is not to focus on the others. Look at your plate, or in the case of a box, the box. Take them one at a time, and focus on getting the food from the fork to your mouth smoothly. Don't leave the fork in the plate between bites either. Dress code anxiety is real, but the best way is usually to be politely confident. If you' not sure, ask how they' like it. Read like you would a book. Pick something, and give it a proper reading. You' usually find something you comfortable with. Definitely. That allows the staff to see you' enjoying yourself, and they' happily help with your meal.",
